          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#monoidal_prederivators Monoidal prederivators
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Dia
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Dia
            be a suitable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            shapes, as used to define
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivators"} derivators
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi PDer
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PDer
            of prederivators is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+category"} functor
            2-category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi Dia
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi CAT
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [Dia^{op},CAT]
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+category"} cartesian
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+2-category"} monoidal 2-category
          %p
            A
            %strong monoidal prederivator
            is simply a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudomonoid"} pseudomonoid
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PDer
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PDer
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Dia
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi MonCat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Dia^{op} \to MonCat
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi MonCat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MonCat
            consists of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+categories"} monoidal categories
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+functors"} monoidal functors
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+natural+transformations"} monoidal natural transformations
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braided+monoidal+category"} braided
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric
            monoidal prederivators.
          %p
            A
            %strong monoidal semiderivator
            is a monoidal prederivator which is a semiderivator.
          %h3#monoidal_derivators Monoidal derivators
          %p We could define a monoidal derivator to be simply a monoidal prederivator which is a derivator. This is what Groth does. However, we might also want to ask that the tensor product be well-behaved with respect to homotopy Kan extensions, and the natural requirement is that it preserve homotopy colimits in each variable.
          %p
            Precisely, let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            be a monoidal prederivator which is a derivator; we say that its tensor product
            %strong preserves homotopy colimits in each variable separately
            if for any
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Dia
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\in Dia
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi r
                    %mo !
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⇆
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi r
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r_! \colon D(A) \leftrightarrows D(*) : r^*
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+adjunction"} Hopf adjunction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\colon A\to *
            is the unique functor to the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+category"} terminal category
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonoidal+adjunction"} comonoidal adjunction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi r
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r^*
            is strong monoidal.
          %p
            Explicitly, this means that for any diagram
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\in D(A)
            and any object
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y\in D(*)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi hocolim
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msup
                    %mi r
                    %mo *
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi hocolim
                    %mi A
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hocolim^A (X \otimes r^* Y) \to (hocolim^A X) \otimes Y
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi hocolim
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi r
                    %mo *
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi hocolim
                    %mi A
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hocolim^A (r^* Y\otimes X) \to Y\otimes (hocolim^A X)
          %p
            are isomorphisms. In this case we say that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %strong monoidal derivator
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#preservation_of_certain_homotopy_kan_extensions Preservation of certain homotopy Kan extensions
          %p
            The above preservation condition, though stated only for colimits, also applies to certain homotopy Kan extensions. If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\colon B\to A
            is any
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opfibration"} opfibration
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mo !
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_! \dashv p^*
            is also a Hopf adjunction as follows. It suffices to show that for any
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\in A
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\in D(B)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y\in D(A)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi a
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mo !
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mo *
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi a
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mo !
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a^* p_! (X\otimes p^* Y) \to a^* (p_! X \otimes Y)
          %p
            is an isomorphism (and dually). But since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            is an opfibration, the square
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi p
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi g
                        %mtd
                          %mi B
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo
                            %mi q
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mi p
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo →
                            %mi a
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{ p^{-1}(a) &amp; \overset{g}{\to} &amp; B \\
                  ^q\downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow^p \\
                  * &amp; \underset{a}{\to} &amp; A }
          %p
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+exact+square"} homotopy exact
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi a
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mo !
                    %mo ≅
                    %msub
                      %mi q
                      %mo !
                    %msup
                      %mi g
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a^* p_! \cong q_! g^*
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi g
                      %mo *
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mo *
                    %mo ≅
                    %msup
                      %mi q
                      %mo *
                    %msup
                      %mi a
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g^* p^* \cong q^* a^*
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi q
                    %mo !
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msup
                    %mi q
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q_! \dashv q^*
            is Hopf, we have
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi a
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mo !
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mo *
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %msub
                    %mi q
                    %mo !
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mo *
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %msub
                    %mi q
                    %mo !
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mo *
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mo *
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mo *
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %msub
                    %mi q
                    %mo !
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mo *
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msup
                    %mi q
                    %mo *
                  %msup
                    %mi a
                    %mo *
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %msub
                    %mi q
                    %mo !
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mo *
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msup
                    %mi a
                    %mo *
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ≅
                  %msup
                    %mi a
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mo !
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msup
                    %mi a
                    %mo *
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ≅
                  %msup
                    %mi a
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mo !
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  a^* p_! (X\otimes p^* Y)
                  \\cong q_! g^* (X \otimes p^* Y)
                  \\cong q_! (g^* X \otimes g^* p^* Y)
                  \\cong q_! (g^* X \otimes q^* a^* Y)
                  \\cong q_! g^* X \otimes a^* Y
                  \\cong a^* p_! X \otimes a^* Y
                  \\cong a^* (p_! X \otimes Y).
          %p We leave it to the reader to verify that this composite isomorphism is, in fact, the transformation in question.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p Any representable prederivator represented by a monoidal category is a monoidal prederivator. If the monoidal category is complete and cocomplete, and its tensor product preserves colimits on each side, then this is a monoidal derivator.
            %li
              %p
                The homotopy derivator of any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"} monoidal model category
                is a monoidal derivator.
